  </ctml:teamMatches>
  <ctml:notes>World Team Rapid Championship: a 12-round Swiss for teams (48 teams, six boards, rapid 15+10) at Queen Elizabeth Stadium, Wan Chai, Hong Kong, 17-19 June 2026. Champion: Dragon Chilling (rank 1). The separately-run World Team BLITZ Championship (pools + knockout, 20-21 June) is a different event and is not in this file. Primary source: the chess.com broadcast PGN (per-move clocks, FIDE ids, teams); team standings and the completeness proof come from the ChessResults Final Ranking crosstable. The builder recomputed every team's match points and game points from the games and every round's pairing, and they reproduce the crosstable exactly for all 48 teams. 7 duplicate game line-items (rounds 1-2) were collapsed by (round, player-pair), keeping the copy with movetext. 84 result-only games (no movetext in the source) are stored without moves. Boards use the source's global per-round numbering; the intra-match board (1-6) is given on each teamMatch board and in each game's source note. Player federations are not in the source PGN, so none are asserted. Uses the CTML 2.1 team model (ctml:teams, ctml:teamMatches, game/@whiteTeam/@blackTeam).</ctml:notes>
  <ctml:source kind="chess.com-pgn">
    <ctml:uri>file:///D:/elysium/sources/twic/2026-fide-world-rapid-team-chess-championship.pgn</ctml:uri>
    <ctml:note>1735 game line-items (1728 after de-duplication); SHA-256 ad7b06c1d1bfd073929837cb73537314492defa5d535c2a3b5b2f6a7f0eee515. Moves, clocks, and results authoritative.</ctml:note>
  </ctml:source>
  <ctml:source kind="chess-results-crosstable">
    <ctml:uri>file:///D:/elysium/sources/twic/2026-fide-world-rapid-team-chess-championship.txt</ctml:uri>
    <ctml:note>Final Ranking crosstable after 12 rounds (tnr 1435703); SHA-256 2e006482ed3cc6f74728c0042d99e777b64181cc2ac19dc2b290bca94886e706. Team standings, tiebreaks, and per-round pairings; completeness proof.</ctml:note>
  </ctml:source>
  <ctml:source kind="fide-rating-list">
    <ctml:uri>file:///D:/elysium/sources/fide/xml-originals/standard_sep26frl_xml.xml</ctml:uri>
    <ctml:note>Official FIDE standard rating list (standard_sep26frl_xml); resolves player federations by FIDE id. SHA-256 24f735101428f10493e951987dac76806643619347cc54e142112e277b5139ff.</ctml:note>
  </ctml:source>
  <ctml:source kind="eco-table">
